  ('legacy:589',589,'Most asylum seekers originating','UNHCR','Displacement · population:coo:asylum_seekers','verified','95','advance_to_validation','clear_generic_legacy_block','broad_intuitive_distinct','Broad, recognizable displacement measure with a distinct player-facing question; the old generic rejection is not a sufficient reason to suppress it.','Use the recovered UNHCR Refugee Data Finder importer; validate coverage/year consistency and then clear the legacy-only blocker.','family:unhcr:most-asylum-seekers-originating','ready_for_source_family_validation'),
  ('legacy:594',594,'Highest cabbage yield','FAOSTAT','Vegetables · QCL:''01212:5412','verified','','retain_exclusion','confirm_reasoned_exclusion','agriculture_item_matrix_overproliferation','The concept comes from the legacy FAOSTAT item-by-element expansion matrix. Even when source-valid, the remaining yield/area/production/animal-count slices add low marginal variety and would re-saturate an already agriculture-heavy catalog; v16.2.6 deliberately prefers a small set of recognizable representative food/agriculture anchors.','Keep excluded from the playable core. Reconsider only if a future category is both highly recognizable and demonstrably distinct from retained crop/livestock/food anchors.','',''),
